<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-sweden"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Sweden.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Sweden</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sweden joins NATO</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/johor-sultanate"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Johor%20Sultanate.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Johor Sultanate</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sultan Ibrahim Iskandar becomes King of Malaysia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-south-africa"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20South%20Africa.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of South Africa</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The ANC loses its majority and forms a Government of National Unity</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-austria"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Austria.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Austria</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">After the election of 29 September, coalition talks collapse and Karl Nehammer resigns; a People's Party, Social Democrat and NEOS coalition under Christian Stocker eventually takes office.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/lebanese-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lebanese%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Lebanese Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Israel invades on 1 October after killing Hezbollah's leader Hassan Nasrallah on 27 September; a ceasefire follows in November.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/syrian-arab-republic"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Syrian%20Arab%20Republic.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Syrian Arab Republic</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 8 December opposition forces led by Hay'at Tahrir al-Sham capture Damascus, ending 53 years of Assad family rule; Bashar al-Assad flees to Moscow.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/georgia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Georgia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Georgia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The disputed election of 26 October and the suspension of EU accession until 2028 plunge the country into crisis; the outgoing president Salome Zourabichvili refuses to recognise her successor.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/singapore"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Singapore.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Singapore</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Lawrence Wong becomes the fourth prime minister on 15 May, the first born after independence; his party wins 65.5 percent and 87 of 97 seats in 2025.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/language/pali"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pali.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pali</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Government of India designates Pali a classical language of India</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/non-aligned-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Non-Aligned%20Movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Non-Aligned Movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The 19th summit meets in Kampala, Uganda</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/pan-arabism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Pan-Arabism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Pan-Arabism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The fall of the Assad regime ends Ba’athist rule in Syria, which had espoused pan-Arabism</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/notre-dame-de-paris"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Notre-Dame%20de%20Paris.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Notre-Dame de Paris</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The restored cathedral reopened in a ceremony on 7 December</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/nazca-lines"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nazca%20Lines.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nazca Lines</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Archaeologists from Yamagata University's Nazca Institute and IBM Research used artificial intelligence to find 303 previously unknown figurative geoglyphs</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/maori-king-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/M%C4%81ori%20King%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Māori King movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Nga wai hono i te po is announced as the eighth monarch after the death of King Tūheitia</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/baathism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Ba'athism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Ba'athism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Assad regime falls on 8 December, ending Ba'athist rule in Syria</span></li></ul></section>
